## Why This Is Asked

Tests a practical NLP task: normalize product names across languages in chat, a common customer-support need.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual dictionary-based normalization
- Code-switching handling via token-level language tagging
- Lightweight fuzzy matching (Levenshtein) for typos
- In-browser latency constraints and basic privacy controls
- Per-language evaluation plan

## Code Example

```javascript
const dict = {
  en: { "iphone": "IPHON-X" },
  es: { "iphone": "IPHON-X" },
  de: { "iphone": "IPHON-X" }
};

function normalize(token, lang){
  const d = dict[lang] || {};
  if (d[token]) return { canonical_id: d[token], conf: 1.0 };
  // simple fallback: lowercasing + basic similarity could be added here
  return { canonical_id: token, conf: 0.5 };
}
```

